[F. County Governments' Compliance with the PFM Act]

 Failure to establish County Budget and Economic Forums: Section 137 of the PFM Act requires Counties to establish, operationalize Budget and Economic Forums as a means of consultation  during  preparation  of  budgets  as  well  as  plans,  Fiscal  Strategy  Papers  and Budget Review and Outlook Papers. A number of Counties have not yet established these forums.

55. The  FY  2016/17  marked  the  end  of  the  initial  four  and  half  years of fiscal decentralization that was followed by August 2017 elections, which marked transition from the first  County  Governments.  Therefore,  the  foregoing  summary  of  fiscal  performance  and compliance with the PFM Act provides important lessons towards improving preparation of Counties' future plans, Fiscal Strategy Papers and budgets as well as their implementation. As part of measures to address the failures highlighted above:

 The National Treasury proposes reintroduction of the PFM Amendment Bill (2015), which lapsed with the eleventh Parliament. The amendments sought to address legal loopholes that give rise to leakages from operation of County bank accounts, as well as delays in County budget approvals, which leads to low absorption;

 A training curriculum is currently being designed under the Kenya School of Government (KSG) targeting  County  Government  officials  with  decision-making  roles  in  budgeting, revenue collection, and financial accounting and reporting;

 A nation-wide capacity building initiative -- Kenya Devolution Support Program (KDSP) - is already being rolled out, with a major focus on usage of IFMIS, procurement and audit, among other problematic PFM aspects;

